<div class="service-block">
	<div class="service-text reveal--left reveal">
		<h3>Individual Therapy</h3>
		<p>
			I offer individual therapy to adolescents and young adults. I specialize in
			treating young people who are experiencing depression, anxiety, trauma
			symptoms, suicidal ideation, and non-suicidal self-harm urges.
		</p>
		<p>
			Individual therapy is a highly collaborative process, from treatment planning  to identifying what therapeutic approaches are best suited for your needs. Although I am an expert in the mental health and social work field, you are the expert on your life, needs, and goals. We will work together to support you with building a life worth living. 
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="service-image">
		<img class="officeimg" src="{{ '/images/office_cropped.jpg' | url | bust }}" alt="">
	</div>
</div>

<hr class="service-divider">

<div class="service-block reverse">
	<div class="service-text reveal--right reveal">
		<h3>Family Therapy</h3>
		<p>
			When working with adolescents, I find that a significant amount of healing
			and progress occurs during family therapy. I view "problems" or
			concerns in the context of a system, meaning somebody's challenges are
			not simply a personal deficit. Rather, issues are complex, multi-faceted, and
			frequently require healing in the context of relationships.
		</p>
		<p>
			Family therapy can occur throughout a child or adolescent's individual treatment (i.e. scheduling only when necessary), or it can be a stand-alone service provided to any family.
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="service-image">
		<img src="{{ '/images/image1.png' | url | bust }}" alt="">
	</div>
</div>

<hr class="service-divider">

